From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Osipenko <digetx@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Jun 2021 19:41:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/45] memory: tegra: Don't error out DMA flushing

DMA flushing may fail if hardware unit is power-gated. We need to reset
hardware unit and its memory clients in a certain order, but it becomes
complicated when we need to power-up hardware domain for the first time
since resets are requested in a special order. We assumed that power
domains are initially turned on all devices, but this could be a wrong
assumption.

This copy adds a comment on the Surface RT case: the 3D2 client never
drains when the PMC powers down unused domains at probe, and without
this tegra-pmc fails to probe, taking USB, PWM, backlight and display
with it.

Rebased to Linux 7.2.13 for linux-surface-rt; from codeberg.org/libre-tegra/linux v7.0.1-stable
8d0f5f4f9fff.

Signed-off-by: Dmitry Osipenko <digetx@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/memory/tegra/mc.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/memory/tegra/mc.c b/drivers/memory/tegra/mc.c
index ec80ea9cc..3d9ffd5e5 100644
--- a/drivers/memory/tegra/mc.c
+++ b/drivers/memory/tegra/mc.c
@@ -263,9 +263,14 @@ static int tegra_mc_hotreset_assert(struct reset_controller_dev *rcdev,
 		/* wait for completion of the outstanding DMA requests */
 		while (!rst_ops->dma_idling(mc, rst)) {
 			if (!retries--) {
-				dev_err(mc->dev, "failed to flush %s DMA\n",
+				/*
+				 * A client that never drains (3D2 on the Surface RT)
+				 * must not fail the hot reset: tegra-pmc would then
+				 * fail to probe and take USB, PWM and display with it.
+				 */
+				dev_dbg(mc->dev, "failed to flush %s DMA\n",
 					rst->name);
-				return -EBUSY;
+				break;
 			}
 
 			usleep_range(10, 100);
-- 
